{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"const RUN_CANCEL_REASON: \"tanstack-ai:cancel-requested\" = 'tanstack-ai:cancel-requested';","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/cancel.ts#L30","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/cancel.ts:30"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Abort reason that marks an abort as an explicit cancellation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Namespaced so an application's own reason string cannot collide with it by\naccident, and matched with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"==="},{"type":"text","value":" (never a substring test) so an arbitrary\nprovider error message can never be read as a deliberate cancel."}]}],"headings":[]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nconst RUN_CANCEL_REASON: \"tanstack-ai:cancel-requested\" = 'tanstack-ai:cancel-requested';\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/cancel.ts:30](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/cancel.ts#L30)\n\nAbort reason that marks an abort as an explicit cancellation.\n\nNamespaced so an application's own reason string cannot collide with it by\naccident, and matched with `===` (never a substring test) so an arbitrary\nprovider error message can never be read as a deliberate cancel.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: RUN_CANCEL_REASON\ntitle: RUN_CANCEL_REASON\n---\n\n```ts\nconst RUN_CANCEL_REASON: \"tanstack-ai:cancel-requested\" = 'tanstack-ai:cancel-requested';\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/cancel.ts:30](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/cancel.ts#L30)\n\nAbort reason that marks an abort as an explicit cancellation.\n\nNamespaced so an application's own reason string cannot collide with it by\naccident, and matched with `===` (never a substring test) so an arbitrary\nprovider error message can never be read as a deliberate cancel.\n"}
